# steam.fk: a steam power plant, 3.6 MW. Plot 16x26. Water from the lake, two boilers burning
# coal, four steam engines; the router lays the water and steam as pipes and the coal as a belt
# with an inserter into each boiler. Place the plot so the pump stands on the shore with water
# west of it (rot 3 faces west). Coal by belt from drills works the same way.
# Run:  fk check steam.fk    fk rates steam.fk    fk build --to report_checks
# Expect: `check steam: 8 machines, 3 nets, 0 check lines`; the boilers at full speed (`steam
# 3600.00` a minute each), the pump at 10%; no check line at all: `steam: 3 poles, on a grid with
# generation` (out\floorplan.txt).
pump = OffshorePump<rate=1200/s>               @(0, 17, rot 3)
b1   = Boiler<fuel=coal>                       @(2, 13)
b2   = Boiler<fuel=coal>                       @(10, 13)
e1   = SteamEngine                             @(2, 0)
e2   = SteamEngine                             @(2, 5)
e3   = SteamEngine                             @(10, 0)
e4   = SteamEngine                             @(10, 5)
coal = Chest<requester, item=coal, rate=1/s>   @(6, 22)

net water: pump -> b1, b2
net steam: b1, b2 -> e1, e2, e3, e4
net fuel:  coal -> b1, b2
